    "body": "## Overview\n\n`MoRIIOConnectorWorker.__init__` re-runs the attention backend selector with the global cache dtype. DeepSeek-V4 sets that dtype to `fp8_ds_mla` at model init, and the selector call passes no `use_sparse`, so no ROCm backend matches and the worker raises at startup. This PR reads the backend from the model's attention layers with `get_current_attn_backends`, as the NIXL and Mooncake workers already do.\n\nIt is the one hunk of #48989 that MoRIIO READ mode needs, split out so it can land on its own.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Fixes the `ValueError: No valid attention backend found` that the MoRIIO worker raises for DeepSeek-V4 on ROCm, for both the producer and the consumer.\n- No behavior change for other models. `backend_name` is only logged and sent as `attn_backend_name` in the handshake metadata, and no code compares it.\n- Unit tests keep the same path: with no registered layers, `get_current_attn_backends` falls back to the same selector call.\n\n## Validation\n\n| Check | main | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| The selector call of `MoRIIOConnectorWorker.__init__`, DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813 config, cache dtype after model init (`fp8_ds_mla`) | `ValueError` (below) | call removed |\n| `test_moriio_connector.py` + `test_moriio_kv_layout.py` + `test_moriio_hma_scheduler.py` (ROCm, MI350X, mori installed) | 185 passed | 185 passed |\n\n```text\nValueError: No valid attention backend found for rocm with AttentionSelectorConfig(head_size=512,\ndtype=torch.bfloat16, kv_cache_dtype=fp8_ds_mla, block_size=None, use_mla=True, has_sink=False,\nuse_sparse=False, ...). Reasons: {ROCM_AITER_MLA: [kv_cache_dtype not supported], TRITON_MLA:\n[kv_cache_dtype not supported], ROCM_AITER_TRITON_MLA: [kv_cache_dtype not supported]}.\n```\n\n<details>\n<summary>Reproducer for the selector call (no model load)</summary>\n\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom vllm.engine.arg_utils import EngineArgs\nfrom vllm.config import set_current_vllm_config\nfrom vllm.v1.attention.selector import get_attn_backend\n\ncfg = EngineArgs(model=sys.argv[1], trust_remote_code=True, kv_cache_dtype=\"fp8\",\n                 max_model_len=8192, enforce_eager=True).create_engine_config()\nmc, cc = cfg.model_config, cfg.cache_config\ncc.cache_dtype = \"fp8_ds_mla\"  # what DeepseekV4 attention sets at model init\nwith set_current_vllm_config(cfg):\n    get_attn_backend(mc.get_head_size(), mc.dtype, cc.cache_dtype, use_mla=mc.use_mla)\n```\n\n</details>\n\n- The unit tests ran in a ROCm 10 vLLM nightly container, with this branch's Python tree on `PYTHONPATH`.\n- Not validated end to end on this branch. Our DeepSeek-V4-Pro 1P1D MoRIIO READ setup (2x MI350X) runs a nightly that carries a local workaround at this call site (retry the selector with `use_sparse=True`). The nodes are not available right now; I will add the E2E result when they are.\n\n## Details\n\n**Flow.**\n1. `DeepseekV4` attention init rewrites `cache_config.cache_dtype` from `fp8` to `fp8_ds_mla` (`vllm/models/deepseek_v4/attention.py`).\n2. `Worker.initialize_from_config` calls `ensure_kv_transfer_initialized`, which builds `MoRIIOConnectorWorker` after the model is loaded.\n3. The worker calls `get_attn_backend(head_size=512, bfloat16, \"fp8_ds_mla\", use_mla=True)` with no `use_sparse`. Every ROCm MLA backend rejects the dtype.\n\nThe layers already hold the backends they selected. `get_current_attn_backends` reads them, so the connector no longer needs to repeat the selection with a partial set of arguments.\n\n**Relation to #48989.** #48989 (@itej89) makes the same backend change, plus CI and Dockerfile updates, a spec-type check, WRITE-mode HMA changes and a `block_len` check removal. READ mode needs only the backend change. `MLAAttentionSpec` subclasses `FullAttentionSpec` and `SlidingWindowMLASpec` subclasses `SlidingWindowSpec`, so main's HMA check already accepts DeepSeek-V4's groups. #48989 has had merge conflicts since 10-15. If this lands first, #48989 can drop the hunk on rebase. @itej89 is credited as co-author.\n\n**Duplicate check.** I searched open PRs for `moriio backend`, `moriio get_attn_backend`, `moriio get_current_attn_backends`, `moriio DeepSeek-V4`, `moriio fp8_ds_mla` and `moriio attention backend`. Only #48989 changes this call site.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\nAI assistance (Claude Code) was used to prepare this change.\n",
